# Start a Cognitive3D session from another node, such as a mission or task
# orchestrator: the Cognitive3D node's `~/start_session` service. It names the
# session, attaches what the caller knows about the task, and returns the
# session's id so the session can be found later.
#
# Sessions exist only while the node is active: a request to a node that is not
# active is refused and opens nothing, so activate it first. With the node's
# `auto_start_session: true`, activation already opened a session, and a request
# is refused naming it until it is ended.
#
# With the node's `remote_variables` on, the call returns once the session's
# remote variables are fetched, which takes up to `remote_variables_timeout_s`.

# Optional. Recorded as the session property `c3d.sessionname`. Empty falls back
# to the `session_name` parameter, and then to the session id, so a session is
# never left carrying the name of the one before it.
string session_name

# Optional. A flat JSON object of session properties, each value keeping its own
# JSON type. Types matter on the wire: the platform indexes numeric session
# properties separately, so a number sent as a string is invisible to a numeric
# filter. A JSON string is recorded as written. Nested objects, arrays and null
# are refused, and so is any key in the `c3d.` namespace, where the SDK records
# its own session properties: a value there would replace the SDK's. The one
# exception is `c3d.remote_variable.*` while the node's `remote_variables` is
# false.
string properties_json

# Optional. The identifier the platform draws this session's A/B arms for, and
# the session's participant id (`c3d.participant.id`). Empty falls back to the
# node's `device_id`, which keeps one robot in one arm of a sticky test for
# good: right for a test across a fleet, wrong for comparing runs. Use a UUID
# per run. The node sends the platform the lowercase hex SHA-256 of this
# string's bytes, so sequential identifiers spread across arms, and records the
# string itself. Longer than 64 bytes is refused before any session opens.
string participant_id
---
# True when this call opened a session.
bool ok

# The session that is now running. On a refusal because one was already
# running, this is that session's id.
#
# Invariant, and callers depend on it: `ok=false` with a non-empty id means
# "already running as this id, and this call did not open it". Every other
# refusal reports an empty id and has opened nothing, so a caller can leave the
# running session alone on the first, and fix the cause and retry on the second.
string session_id

# Empty on success; on a refusal, what went wrong and what to do about it.
string message

# The remote variables and A/B arms resolved for this session, as a flat JSON
# object keyed by variable name with each value keeping its wire type
# ({"nav_speed_centimeters_per_second":30}). "{}" when nothing is configured for
# this identifier. Empty when the fetch is off (`remote_variables: false`) or
# failed. A failed fetch also leaves a `c3d.remote_variables.unavailable` event
# in the session; a fetch that is off leaves nothing.
string remote_variables_json
